WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/components/motion/FadeIn.tsx — a transparent MOTION wrapper, not a data surface:
    FadeIn({ children, delay = 0, className = '' }):
      const { reduce, durationMs } = useMotionPreference(400)   // reduce = useReducedMotion() ?? false
                                                                // durationMs = reduce ? 0 : 400
      <motion.div
        initial   = {reduce ? false : { opacity: 0, y: 12 }}    // reduce ⇒ render final state, no entry
        animate   = {{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}
        transition= {{ duration: durationMs/1000, delay: reduce ? 0 : delay, ease: 'easeOut' }} >
        {children}
      </motion.div>
  Its ONLY data dependency is useMotionPreference; it renders no copy of its own ("anonymous").
  Its ONLY branches are the two motion states (animated entry / reduced-motion instant settle). The
  generic loading/empty/error/stale/offline states belong to whatever content the caller embeds —
  identical to the sanctioned disposition for the pure-presentational ToolCard surface (P-0010).

