PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported)
  useMotionPreference(400)   → FadeInMotionInput.webDefaultDurationMs = 400 + FadeInMotionProjection
  reduce = useReducedMotion()→ @Environment(\.accessibilityReduceMotion), threaded to the model; the web
                               `?? false` coalescing is reproduced by FadeInMotionInput.make(reduceMotion: Bool?).
  initial {opacity:0,y:12}   → plan.initialOpacity 0 / initialOffsetY 12 (points) ; reduce ⇒ 1 / 0 (final)
  animate {opacity:1,y:0}    → plan.finalOpacity 1 / finalOffsetY 0
  transition easeOut dur/del → FadeInAnimationFactory.entrance = .easeOut(duration:).delay(delaySeconds)
  i18n      : surface is anonymous (renders no copy); zero English literals in code — preview/demo strings
              resolve through the FadeInStrings P1/S10 facade (NSLocalizedString table "FadeIn", value: fallback).
  a11y      : transparent wrapper — adds NO accessibility element; children keep their labels/traits (web
              motion.div has no ARIA role). Under reduced motion content is presented opaque immediately, so AT
              never observes a transient hidden state. Honors Reduce Motion + Dynamic Type (token fonts).
  telemetry : view.opened surface="FadeIn" via FadeInModel.start → FadeInTelemetry (P1/S11), default os_log sink.

